  "note": "Election of the rural district council by proportional representation in two electoral areas, 1920 (polled 5 June 1920). First-preference figures not filed (see notes). Elected by proportional representation in the order Cooney, Best, Elliott, Reside, M'Keown (Cooney on the first count, M'Keown on the final count without the quota). Electorate 2,640, valid votes 1,775, quota 296. Counted on Tuesday 8 June 1920 by W. R. Bell, returning officer. Kenny and Lockhart were eliminated on the second count. Labels printed for the elected only."
